    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d424">

                <pb facs="0561" n="481" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg481"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sickles to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-06-28"><hi rendition="#italic">June 28,
                        1901</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 507.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to confirm my telegram of
                    the 27th instant.</p>
                <p>In connection with this matter I inclose herewith, for the consideration of the
                    Department, copies of two letters from the consul-general at Barcelona which
                    will explain Mr. Lay’s uncertainty as to the registration of Cubans and Porto
                    Ricans at that place.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stanton Sickles</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d424-a1.xml" xpointer="d424-a1"/>
